{
 "id": "084-suyun-ustundeki-renkler",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "Colours on the Water",
 "theme": "The art of ebru (paper marbling) and working slowly, with patience",
 "blurb": "On a rainy day, Grandma shows Elif how to paint on water: ebru, the art of marbling. When Elif rushes, the paints mix like mud; Elif takes a deep breath, finds her “snail hands” and patiently makes her own ebru with tulips.",
 "voiceNames": {
  "elif": "Elif",
  "nine": "Grandma (Elif's grandma)",
  "tarcin": "Cinnamon (cat)"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "Outside, the rain went pitter patter. On the window, a snail was crawling slowly, slowly. Elif's grandma put a tray of special water on the table. “Today we're going to paint on water, Elif. It's called ebru.” Elif giggled. “You can't paint on water! It runs away!” Cinnamon the cat jumped onto the table too.",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "Today we're going to paint on water!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "You can't paint on water!"
    },
    "salyangoz": {
     "say": "Slowly, slowly, nice and slow…"
    },
    "tarcin": {
     "say": "Meow? Is that water?"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch the snail on the window!",
   "ask": "Do you think you can paint on water? How would it work?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Elif grabbed the brush. Splat! Splat! Splat! She flicked the paints on fast, fast. Paint splashed everywhere. The colours sank to the bottom and mixed like mud. Even Cinnamon the cat ran away! Elif's cheeks went hot. “It's ruined! It's not nice at all!”",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "It's ruined! It's not nice at all!"
    },
    "tarcin": {
     "say": "Meoooww!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Elif!",
   "ask": "Why did Elif get cross? How do you feel when something doesn't turn out the way you wanted?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Grandma came over. “Cross, aren't you? I was cross at my first ebru too. Water doesn't like hurry, my lamb.” Elif breathed in deeply through her nose. She breathed out slowly through her mouth. Then she saw the snail on the window. Her eyes lit up. She had an idea!",
   "hits": {
    "nine": {
     "say": "Water doesn't like hurry, my lamb."
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "In through my nose… out through my mouth. Ahh."
    },
    "tarcin": {
     "say": "Purrr…"
    },
    "salyangoz": {
     "say": "Slowly, slowly, nice and slow…"
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think Elif's idea was?",
    "res": "Good guess! Let's see.",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "Painting slowly like a snail"
     },
     {
      "l": "Watching Grandma first"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Breathe with Elif!",
   "ask": "What did Elif do to calm down? Let's breathe in through our nose and out through our mouth too."
  },
  {
   "text": "“My snail hands are here!” said Elif. She shook the brush slowly, slowly. Drip! Red. Drip! Yellow. Drip! Blue. Drip! Pink. Drip! Green. The drops didn't sink. They spread out in round circles on the water.",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "My snail hands are here!"
    },
    "nine": {
     "say": "That's it, slowly, slowly."
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Five drops, five coloured circles!",
    "msg": "Five colours!"
   },
   "hint": "Count the drops one by one!",
   "ask": "Which colours did Elif drip? Which colour would you like to drip?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Elif pulled the colours with the brush handle. The red circles became tulips! Grandma handed her a white paper. Elif laid it on the water. “One… two… three…” No hurry. Then she took the paper by its edge and slowly lifted it.",
   "hits": {
    "firca": {
     "say": "Pull… pull… it's a tulip!"
    },
    "kagit": {
     "say": "Here, my lamb, white paper."
    },
    "tepsi": {
     "say": "One… two… three… No hurry!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Now lift it slowly and see!",
    "msg": "You did it in order!"
   },
   "hint": "Touch Elif's brush!",
   "ask": "In what order did Elif make the ebru? What came first, then what, and what came last?"
  },
  {
   "text": "The colours were dancing on the paper! Red tulips, blue waves, yellow speckles. Elif's heart went flutter, flutter. Cinnamon came back too. “Purrr!” he sniffed the tulips. “Grandma, my snail hands made this!” Grandma laughed. “You waited for the water. And the water gave you flowers.”",
   "hits": {
